# Rust Cargo Planner

`Lux.Rust.CargoPlanner` builds deterministic package-management plans for Lux
Rust projects. It does not run Cargo directly; it returns manifest, dependency,
build, version, and cache data that callers can execute or persist.

```elixir
alias Lux.Rust.CargoPlanner

plan =
  CargoPlanner.plan(
    name: "lux_native",
    dependencies: %{
      serde: "~> 1.0",
      serde_json: "1",
      rustler: "^0.36"
    },
    version_index: %{
      "serde" => ["1.0.197"],
      "serde_json" => ["1.0.115"],
      "rustler" => ["0.36.2"]
    },
    features: %{default: ["serde/derive"]},
    profile: :release,
    build_features: ["nif", "serde"]
  )

plan.cargo_toml
plan.resolved_dependencies
plan.build
plan.cache
```

The planner can also summarize a `Cargo.lock` file:

```elixir
"priv/rust/Cargo.lock"
|> File.read!()
|> CargoPlanner.parse_lock()
```

Use `CargoPlanner.dependency_conflicts/1` before writing manifests when generated
dependencies come from multiple Lux components.
